  "description": "HiQPdf Library for .NET (Classic New Generation) is a fast and flexible tool for creating complex and high-quality PDF documents in applications targeting .NET Framework, .NET Core and .NET Standard on Windows.\n\nThe New Generation (NG) uses an improved rendering engine to convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG, with support for ECMAScript 6, WOFF 2, HTTP/2 and TLS 1.3.\n\nThe HiQPdf API runs on the Chromium engine of HiQPdf Next in the HiQPdf.Windows, HiQPdf.Linux and HiQPdf.MacOS packages, without code changes.\n\nFor Windows, Linux and macOS, on x64 and ARM64, HiQPdf Next offers a newer Chromium-based rendering engine for modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript in the multi-platform package HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf and in the platform packages HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows, HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux, HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.MacOS.\n\nThe full HiQPdf Next library, which also converts Word, Excel, RTF and Markdown to PDF, comes in the HiQPdf.Next, HiQPdf.Next.Windows, HiQPdf.Next.Windows.Arm64, HiQPdf.Next.Linux, HiQPdf.Next.Linux.Arm64 and HiQPdf.Next.MacOS packages.\n\nMigration guide from Classic to Next:\nhttps://www.hiqpdf.com/hiqpdf-classic-to-next-migration\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* .NET Framework 4.0 and above\n* .NET 10, 9, 8, 7, 6 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Windows platforms\n* Azure Cloud Services and Azure Virtual Machines\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nLibrary Features:\n\n* Convert HTML to PDF, images and SVG\n* Convert PDF pages to images and HTML\n* Extract text and images from PDF documents\n* Search text in PDF documents\n* Create PDF documents with text, HTML, SVG, images and graphics\n* Create encrypted, password-protected, digitally signed PDF documents\n* Create PDF documents with forms, text notes, links and JavaScript actions\n* Merge multiple PDF documents into a single one\n* Stamp PDF with HTML, text and images",
